    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>RAII handle for a C FILE*.</para>
<para>The purpose of using the C IO interface instead of iostreams is that the former is faster to a ridiculous degree. This class wraps the C IO interface to be more useful in a C++ context. For example the file is automatically closed in the destructor and if the file cannot be opened then an exception is thrown instead of returning a null pointer. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
